# Infrastructure Patterns (SST + AWS)

## SST is the only way to define infrastructure

Never use raw AWS CDK constructs directly. Never click through the AWS console to create resources. All infrastructure is defined in the `/infra` directory as SST code, committed to the repo.

## SST basics

```typescript
// sst.config.ts
export default $config({
  app(input) {
    return {
      name: "research-platform",
      removal: input?.stage === "production" ? "retain" : "remove",
      home: "aws",
    };
  },
  async run() {
    // Import and instantiate stacks
    const db = await import("./infra/database");
    const storage = await import("./infra/storage");
    const api = await import("./infra/api");
    const frontend = await import("./infra/frontend");
  },
});
```

## Secrets — always use AWS Secrets Manager

```typescript
// infra/secrets.ts
export const anthropicApiKey = new sst.Secret("AnthropicApiKey");
export const dbPassword = new sst.Secret("DatabasePassword");

// Reference in API
const api = new sst.aws.Function("Api", {
  link: [anthropicApiKey, dbPassword],  // SST injects as env vars at runtime
  ...
});
```

## Environment variables via Parameter Store

```typescript
// For non-sensitive config
const config = new aws.ssm.Parameter("AppConfig", {
  name: "/research-platform/production/config",
  type: "String",
  value: JSON.stringify({ maxThreadsPerTask: 50, defaultWorkingLanguage: "en" }),
});
```

## Database

```typescript
// infra/database.ts
export const db = new sst.aws.Postgres("Database", {
  vpc,
  scaling: { min: "0.5 ACU", max: "4 ACU" },  // Aurora Serverless v2
});

// Enable pgvector via migration — don't try to enable via SST
// In your first Alembic migration:
// op.execute("CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector")
```

## SQS queues

```typescript
// infra/queues.ts
export const documentProcessingQueue = new sst.aws.Queue("DocumentProcessing", {
  transform: {
    queue: {
      visibilityTimeoutSeconds: 300,  // 5 min — enough for large document processing
      messageRetentionSeconds: 86400, // 1 day
    }
  }
});

export const workflowExecutionQueue = new sst.aws.Queue("WorkflowExecution", {
  transform: {
    queue: {
      visibilityTimeoutSeconds: 600,  // 10 min — workflows can be long
    }
  }
});
```

## S3 storage

```typescript
// infra/storage.ts
export const documentsBucket = new sst.aws.Bucket("Documents", {
  transform: {
    bucket: {
      versioning: { status: "Enabled" },  // Always enabled — protects against accidental deletion
    }
  }
});
```

## SST dev mode — local development

```bash
# Start SST dev mode — connects local code to real AWS services
npx sst dev

# This:
# - Connects your local Next.js and Python code to real Bedrock, S3, SQS
# - Hot-reloads on code changes
# - No LocalStack, no mocking
# - Requires AWS credentials configured (use AWS SSO or ~/.aws/credentials)
```

## CloudWatch alerts via SST

```typescript
// infra/monitoring.ts
// Error rate alarm
new aws.cloudwatch.MetricAlarm("ErrorRateAlarm", {
  metricName: "5XXError",
  namespace: "ResearchPlatform/API",
  statistic: "Sum",
  period: 300,  // 5 minutes
  threshold: 10,
  comparisonOperator: "GreaterThanThreshold",
  alarmActions: [snsAlertTopic.arn],
});
```

## Alembic database migrations

All schema changes via Alembic migrations. Never modify the database directly.

```bash
# Create a new migration
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add workflow_execution table"

# Apply migrations (runs automatically on deploy via GitHub Actions)
alembic upgrade head

# First migration must enable pgvector
# alembic/versions/001_initial.py
def upgrade():
    op.execute("CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector")
    op.create_table("tasks", ...)
```

## GitHub Actions — deploy to production

```yaml
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Configure AWS credentials
        uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v4
        with:
          role-to-assume: ${{ secrets.AWS_DEPLOY_ROLE_ARN }}
          aws-region: us-east-1
      - name: Run migrations
        run: poetry run alembic upgrade head
      - name: Deploy with SST
        run: npx sst deploy --stage production
```

## Domain and SSL

```typescript
// infra/frontend.ts
export const frontend = new sst.aws.Nextjs("Frontend", {
  domain: {
    name: "app.yourplatform.com",  // Update with actual domain
    dns: sst.aws.dns(),            // Route 53
  },
  // SSL via ACM is automatic with SST domain config
});
```

## Cost management — always set budget alerts

Budget alerts are defined outside SST (via AWS console or boto3 during initial setup):
- Total monthly: warn at $50, critical at $100
- Bedrock specifically: warn at $30
- EC2 + RDS: warn at $20
- Cost Anomaly Detection: enabled always

## EC2 dev server

The development environment runs on EC2, not your local machine. To connect:

```bash
# SSH into dev server
ssh -i ~/.ssh/research-platform-dev.pem ubuntu@<EC2_IP>

# Or configure in ~/.ssh/config
Host research-dev
  HostName <EC2_IP>
  User ubuntu
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/research-platform-dev.pem

# Then connect via Cursor: Cmd+Shift+P → "Remote-SSH: Connect to Host" → research-dev
```

The EC2 instance runs:
- OrbStack with PostgreSQL + pgvector container
- SST dev mode connecting to real AWS Bedrock, S3, SQS
- All development tools (Node.js, Python, Poetry, pnpm)
- The development environment is Linux Ubuntu 24 LTS — all paths and commands are Linux
